<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<map xmlns="http://openorienteering.org/apps/mapper/xml/v2" version="9">
    <notes>INFO (course setter to include on map)
Title: Hillmorton High
Scale: 1:4,000
Contour interval: 2.5m
North lines: 120m apart


CREDITS (course setter to include on map - 6pt Arial)
Cartography: E. Musgrave 2023
Copyright © Peninsula and Plains Orienteers
Possession of this map does not imply right of access
Non-commercial use only unless otherwise granted
Map version: f5e350a


COORDINATORS' NOTES (map coordinator to update + commit on map being sent)
Last sent to: Malcolm Ingham &lt;mandg.ingham@xtra.co.nz&gt;


CONTROLLERS' NOTES (controller to read upon map being sent)


MAPPERS' NOTES
 Following Hillmorton JWOC trials 2023 several issues with the map were noted but have been corrected:
 - Increase line spacing on stairs to match the 0.4mm ISSOM limit - this probably requires reducing step count in a few places, but this is certainly legal.
 - Increasing the building to building spacing to meet the 0.4mm limit.
 - rethink the mapping of fences and gates
 - update to include the missing gate in the tennis courts
 - update to include the new accessible playground that has been added
 - Ensure canopy mapping is consistent - sometimes refers to shade sails I think.
 - Consistency with man made feature symbol usage
 - Change how the plots of trees on the field are mapped
 - Fix what I believe to be incorrect usage of the stone wall symbol in a number of places.
 - Check mapping of tree canopies and small/large tree symbols.
(David Wright)</notes>
